    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-10",
      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Backline check",
          "heading": "Vinaya Habosi beats four defenders for Fiji try in France loss",
          "body": "Centre Vinaya Habosi beat four defenders to score, one of Fiji's two tries in Saturday's 54-17 defeat in Lyon. Selestino Ravutaumada added a second consolation try, but coach Jake White's side, who started with 10 France-based players including their entire backline, slumped to a fourth straight defeat in the inaugural Nations Championship. Their backs struggled to fire, and Jiuta Wainiqolo, playing in his adopted home, was unable to make an impact."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England injury doubts for Feyi-Waboso and Atkinson before Japan",
          "body": "Wallabies lose Isaac Henry to hamstring strain for rest of November. South Africa without Pollard, Etzebeth and Kolbe for France test."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-10",
      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Borthwick fears Feyi-Waboso and Atkinson may miss Japan test after Wallabies win",
          "body": "Injury news keeps coming for England before Saturday's meeting with Japan. Immanuel Feyi-Waboso hurt an ankle in the first half against Australia, was replaced at half-time and was later seen in a moon boot, while Seb Atkinson came off with a hip problem after the break. Head coach Steve Borthwick said of Atkinson: \"We're talking days to recover, maybe not available next weekend, but it's really too early for me to say that.\" Both men had already missed England's pre-Nations Championship alignment camp while rehabilitating."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Fiji 54-17 ahead of Springboks test",
          "body": "Wallabies lose Isaac Henry to hamstring strain for rest of November. South Africa without Pollard, Etzebeth and Kolbe for France test."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-10",
      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Half-back concerns",
          "heading": "Dupont and Lucu struggle to link at half-back before Springboks test",
          "body": "Antoine Dupont and Maxime Lucu struggled to build a rhythm at half-back in France's 54-17 win over Fiji, losing possession and rarely getting long phases together. Lucu said France lost plenty of ball in the first half, often at the third or fourth ruck, which stopped them setting up their game. He credited Dupont with well-timed switches in the smaller channels, a plan the pair had targeted before the match. Rugbyrama says the combination must be sorted before France face South Africa on Friday."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England injury doubts for Feyi-Waboso and Atkinson before Japan",
          "body": "Wallabies lose Isaac Henry to hamstring strain for rest of November."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-10",
      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Back-row patience",
          "heading": "Nick Timoney says he is grateful for Ireland starts after long wait",
          "body": "Ulster back row Nick Timoney says the long wait for Ireland chances has made him value every appearance. The 31-year-old debuted against the USA in 2021 but added only two caps in the next four years amid a crowded back row; this year he has played all nine Ireland matches across the Six Nations and Nations Championship, three as a starter. He told BBC Sport NI: \"I'm grateful for it and trying not to think too big picture about it.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Fiji 54-17 ahead of Springboks test",
